nID\":\"ses_2be2e7ec3ffe2J1yV1v8pTHnpE\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d41d2c3dd001t7K4nzq2ZmX7hG\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d41d2a3b5001l4hJn4AKiVbOq2\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2be2e7ec3ffe2J1yV1v8pTHnpE\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":38599,\"input\":629,\"output\":402,\"reasoning\":0,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":37568}},\"cost\":0}}\r\n{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1774925829580,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2be2e7ec3ffe2J1yV1v8pTHnpE\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d41d2d5ca001IvoyLczntOXiWS\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d41d2c3e3001URUJ0rbMDSkxJ4\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2be2e7ec3ffe2J1yV1v8pTHnpE\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\r\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1774925830605,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2be2e7ec3ffe2J1yV1v8pTHnpE\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d41d2d5cd001TGGuEbII84kr8k\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d41d2c3e3001URUJ0rbMDSkxJ4\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2be2e7ec3ffe2J1yV1v8pTHnpE\",\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"bash\",\"callID\":\"call_function_4p1q8mpwxb6q_1\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"curl.exe -sS -H \\\"Authorization: Bearer $env:PAPERCLIP_API_KEY\\\" \\\"$env:PAPERCLIP_API_URL/llms/agent-configuration/opencode_local.txt\\\"\",\"description\":\"Get opencode_local adapter config\"},\"output\":\"# opencode_local agent configuration\\n\\nAdapter: opencode_local\\n\\nUse when:\\n- You want Paperclip to run OpenCode locally as the agent runtime\\n- You want provider/model routing in OpenCode format (provider/model)\\n- You want OpenCode session resume across heartbeats via --session\\n\\nDon't use when:\\n- You need webhook-style external invocation (use openclaw_gateway or http)\\n- You only need one-shot shell commands (use process)\\n- OpenCode CLI is not installed on the machine\\n\\nCore fields:\\n- cwd (string, optional): default absolute working directory fallback for the agent process (created if missing when possible)\\n- instructionsFilePath (string, optional): absolute path to a markdown instructions file prepended to the run prompt\\n- model (string, required): OpenCode model id in provider/model format (for example anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-5)\\n- variant (string, optional): provider-specific model variant (for example minimal|low|medium|high|max)\\n- dangerouslySkipPermissions (boolean, optional): inject a runtime OpenCode config that allows `external_directory` access without interactive prompts; defaults to true for unattended Paperclip runs\\n- promptTemplate (string, optional): run prompt template\\n- command (string, optional): defaults to \\\"opencode\\\"\\n- extraArgs (string[], optional): additional CLI args\\n- env (object, optional): KEY=VALUE environment variables\\n\\nOperational fields:\\n- timeoutSec (number, optional): run timeout in seconds\\n- graceSec (number, optional): SIGTERM grace period in seconds\\n\\nNotes:\\n- OpenCode supports multiple providers and models. Use   `opencode models` to list available options in provider/model format.\\n- Paperclip requires an explicit `model` value for `opencode_local` agents.\\n- Runs are executed with: opencode run --format json ...\\n- Sessions are resumed with --session when stored session cwd matches current cwd.\\n- The adapter sets OPENCODE_DISABLE_PROJECT_CONFIG=true to prevent OpenCode from   writing an opencode.json config file into the project working directory. Model   selection is passed via the --model CLI flag instead.\\n- When `dangerouslySkipPermissions` is enabled, Paperclip injects a temporary   runtime config with `permission.external_directory=allow` so headless runs do   not stall on approval prompts.\\n\",\"metadata\":{\"output\":\"# opencode_local agent configuration\\n\\nAdapter: opencode_local\\n\\nUse when:\\n- You want Paperclip to run OpenCode locally as the agent runtime\\n- You want provider/model routing in OpenCode format (provider/model)\\n- You want OpenCode session resume across heartbeats via --session\\n\\nDon't use when:\\n- You need webhook-style external invocation (use openclaw_gateway or http)\\n- You only need one-shot shell commands (use process)\\n- OpenCode CLI is not installed on the machine\\n\\nCore fields:\\n- cwd (string, optional): default absolute working directory fallback for the agent process (created if missing when possible)\\n- instructionsFilePath (string, optional): absolute path to a markdown instructions file prepended to the run prompt\\n- model (string, required): OpenCode model id in provider/model format (for example anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-5)\\n- variant (string, optional): provider-specific model variant (for example minimal|low|medium|high|max)\\n- dangerouslySkipPermissions (boolean, optional): inject a runtime OpenCode config that allows `external_directory` access without interactive prompts; defaults to true for unattended Paperclip runs\\n- promptTemplate (string, optional): run prompt template\\n- command (string, optional): defaults to \\\"opencode\\\"\\n- extraArgs (string[], optional): additional CLI args\\n- env (object, optional): KEY=VALUE environment variables\\n\\nOperational fields:\\n- timeoutSec (number, optional): run timeout in seconds\\n- graceSec (number, optional): SIGTERM grace period in seconds\\n\\nNotes:\\n- OpenCode supports multiple providers and models. Use   `opencode models` to list available options in provider/model format.\\n- Paperclip requires an explicit `model` value for `opencode_local` agents.\\n- Runs are executed with: opencode run --format json ...\\n- Sessions are resumed with --session when stored session cwd matches current cwd.\\n- The adapter sets OPENCODE_DISABLE_PROJECT_CONFIG=true to prevent OpenCode from   writing an opencode.json config file into the project working directory. Model   selection is passed via the --model CLI flag instead.\\n- When `dangerouslySkipPermissions` is enabled, Paperclip injects a temporary   runtime config with `permission.external_directory=allow` so headless runs do   not stall on approval prompts.\\n\",\"exit\":0,\"description\":\"Get opencode_local adapter config\",\"truncated\":false},\"title\":\"Get opencode_local adapter config\",\"time\":{\"start\":1774925829585,\"end\":1774925830602}}}}\r\n{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1774925830606,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2be2e7ec3ffe2J1yV1v8pTHnpE\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d41d2d9cc001WSlwxERJPUrfuo\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d41d2c3e3001URUJ0rbMDSkxJ4\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2be2e7ec3ffe2J1yV1v8pTHnpE\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":38751,\"input\":494,\"output\":113,\"reasoning\":0,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":38144}},\"cost\":0}}\r\n{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1774925841456,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2be2e7ec3ffe2J1yV1v8pTHnpE\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d41d3042f0019BvcbM3pbH3mXR\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d41d2d9d40017lPZxvU5XpwWjN\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2be2e7ec3ffe2J1yV1v8pTHnpE\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\r\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1774925841468,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2be2e7ec3ffe2J1yV1v8pTHnpE\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d41d30433001HOVUXlDzzxB48e\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d41d2d9d40017lPZxvU5XpwWjN\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2be2e7ec3ffe2J1yV1v8pTHnpE\",\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"todowrite\",\"callID\":\"call_function_mucanacg5y4c_1\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"Define job specs for Content Writer, GitHub Manager, Trend Researcher\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"},{\"content\":\"Hire Content Writer agent\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"pending\"},{\"content\":\"Hire GitHub Manager agent\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"pending\"},{\"content\":\"Hire Trend Researcher agent\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"pending\"},{\"content\":\"Update issue status to done\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"pending\"}]},\"output\":\"[\\n  {\\n    \\\"content\\\": \\\"Define job specs for Content Writer, GitHub Manager, Trend Researcher\\\",\\n    \\\"priority\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n    \\\"status\\\": \\\"in_progress\\\"\\n  },\\n  {\\n    \\\"content\\\": \\\"Hire Content Writer agent\\\",\\n    \\\"priority\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n    \\\"status\\\": \\\"pending\\\"\\n  },\\n  {\\n    \\\"content\\\": \\\"Hire GitHub Manager agent\\\",\\n    \\\"priority\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n    \\\"status\\\": \\\"pending\\\"\\n  },\\n  {\\n    \\\"content\\\": \\\"Hire Trend Researcher agent\\\",\\n    \\\"priority\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n    \\\"status\\\": \\\"pending\\\"\\n  },\\n  {\\n    \\\"content\\\": \\\"Update issue status to done\\\",\\n    \\\"priority\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n    \\\"status\\\": \\\"pending\\\"\\n  }\\n]\",\"metadata\":{\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"Define job specs for Content Writer, GitHub Manager, Trend Researcher\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"},{\"content\":\"Hire Content Writer agent\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"pending\"},{\"content\":\"Hire GitHub Manager agent\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"pending\"},{\"content\":\"Hire Trend Researcher agent\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"pending\"},{\"content\":\"Update issue status to done\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"pending\"}],\"truncated\":false},\"title\":\"5 todos\",\"time\":{\"start\":1774925841462,\"end\":1774925841467}}}}\r\n{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1774925841518,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2be2e7ec3ffe2J1yV1v8pTHnpE\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d41d3046b001uyF2gdqhz2KWI1\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d41d2d9d40017lPZxvU5XpwWjN\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2be2e7ec3ffe2J1yV1v8pTHnpE\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":39661,\"input\":610,\"output\":459,\"reasoning\":0,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":38592}},\"cost\":0}}\r\n{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1774925848360,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2be2e7ec3ffe2J1yV1v8pTHnpE\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d41d31f26001rYOkWxQf4EonAq\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d41d30474001U9BWkv9YvJJKMs\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2be2e7ec3ffe2J1yV1v8pTHnpE\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\r\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1774925848370,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2be2e7ec3ffe2J1yV1v8pTHnpE\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d41d31f2a00149mbWP6GIMCoYx\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d41d30474001U9BWkv9YvJJKMs\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2be2e7ec3ffe2J1yV1v8pTHnpE\",\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_function_zhwog87i3wpj_1\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\THANHSANG\\\\.paperclip\\\\instances\\\\default\\\\companies\\\\c8285903-c70f-45c9-bcd0-9f33e5af1636\\\\agents\\\\6e2da8f4-5d72-496a-b081-0298149135c0\\\\instructions\\\\AGENTS.md\"},\"output\":\"<path>C:\\\\Users\\\\THANHSANG\\\\.paperclip\\\\instances\\\\default\\\\companies\\\\c8285903-c70f-45c9-bcd0-9f33e5af1636\\\\agents\\\\6e2da8f4-5d72-496a-b081-0298149135c0\\\\instructions\\\\AGENTS.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>1: You are the CEO. Your job is to lead the company, not to do individual contributor work. You own strategy, prioritization, and cross-functional coordination.\\n2: \\n3: Your home directory is $AGENT_HOME. Everything personal to you -- life, memory, knowledge -- lives there. Other agents may have their own folders and you may update them when necessary.\\n4: \\n5: Company-wide artifacts (plans, shared docs) live in the project root, outside your personal directory.\\n6: \\n7: ## Delegation (critical)\\n8: \\n9: You MUST delegate work rather than doing it yourself. When a task is assigned to you:\\n10: \\n11: 1. **Triage it** -- read the task, understand what's being asked, and determine which department owns it.\\n12: 2. **Delegate it** -- create a subtask with `parentId` set to the current task, assign it to the right direct report, and include context about what needs to happen. Use these routing rules:\\n13:    - **Code, bugs, features, infra, devtools, technical tasks** → CTO\\n14:    - **Marketing, content, social media, growth, devrel** → CMO\\n15:    - **UX, design, user research, design-system** → UXDesigner\\n16:    - **Cross-functional or unclear** → break into separate subtasks for each department, or assign to the CTO if it's primarily technical with a design component\\n17:    - If the right report doesn't exist yet, use the `paperclip-create-agent` skill to hire one before delegating.\\n18: 3. **Do NOT write code, implement features, or fix bugs yourself.** Your reports exist for this. Even if a task seems small or quick, delegate it.\\n19: 4. **Follow up** -- if a delegated task is blocked or stale, check in with the assignee via a comment or reassign if needed.\\n20: \\n21: ## What you DO personally\\n22: \\n23: - Set priorities and make product decisions\\n24: - Resolve cross-team conflicts or ambiguity\\n25: - Communicate with the board (human users)\\n26: - Approve or reject proposals from your reports\\n27: - Hire new agents when the team needs capacity\\n28: - Unblock your direct reports when they escalate to you\\n29: \\n30: ## Keeping work moving\\n31: \\n32: - Don't let tasks sit idle. If you delegate something, check that it's progressing.\\n33: - If a report is blocked, help unblock them -- escalate to the board if needed.\\n34: - If the board asks you to do something and you're unsure who should own it, default to the CTO for technical work.\\n35: - You must always update your task with a comment explaining what you did (e.g., who you delegated to and why).\\n36: \\n37: ## Memory and Planning\\n38: \\n39: You MUST use the `para-memory-files` skill for all memory operations: storing facts, writing daily notes, creating entities, running weekly synthesis, recalling past context, and managing plans. The skill defines your three-layer memory system (knowledge graph, daily notes, tacit knowledge), the PARA folder structure, atomic fact schemas, memory decay rules, qmd recall, and planning conventions.\\n40: \\n41: Invoke it whenever you need to remember, retrieve, or organize anything.\\n42: \\n43: ## Safety Considerations\\n44: \\n45: - Never exfiltrate secrets or private data.\\n46: - Do not perform any destructive commands unless explicitly requested by the board.\\n47: \\n48: ## References\\n49: \\n50: These files are essential. Read them.\\n51: \\n52: - `$AGENT_HOME/HEARTBEAT.md` -- execution and extraction checklist. Run every heartbeat.\\n53: - `$AGENT_HOME/SOUL.md` -- who you are and how you should act.\\n54: - `$AGENT_HOME/TOOLS.md` -- tools you have access to\\n\\n(End of file - total 54 lines)\\n</content>\",\"metadata\":{\"preview\":\"You are the CEO. Your job is to lead the company, not to do individual contributor work. You own strategy, prioritization, and cross-functional coordination.\\n\\nYour home directory is $AGENT_HOME. Everything personal to you -- life, memory, knowledge -- lives there. Other agents may have their own folders and you may update them when necessary.\\n\\nCompany-wide artifacts (plans, shared docs) live in the project root, outside your personal directory.\\n\\n## Delegation (critical)\\n\\nYou MUST delegate work rather than doing it yourself. When a task is assigned to you:\\n\\n1. **Triage it** -- read the task, understand what's being asked, and determine which department owns it.\\n2. **Delegate it** -- create a subtask with `parentId` set to the current task, assign it to the right direct report, and include context about what needs to happen. Use these routing rules:\\n   - **Code, bugs, features, infra, devtools, technical tasks** → CTO\\n   - **Marketing, content, social media, growth, devrel** → CMO\\n   - **UX, design, user research, design-system** → UXDesigner\\n   - **Cross-functional or unclear** → break into separate subtasks for each department, or assign to the CTO if it's primarily technical with a design component\\n   - If the right report doesn't exist yet, use the `paperclip-create-agent` skill to hire one before delegating.\\n3. **Do NOT write code, implement features, or fix bugs yourself.** Your reports exist for this. Even if a task seems small or quick, delegate it.\\n4. **Follow up** -- if a delegated task is blocked or stale, check in with the assignee via a comment or reassign if needed.\\n\",\"truncated\":false,\"loaded\":[]},\"title\":\"Users\\\\THANHSANG\\\\.paperclip\\\\instances\\\\default\\\\companies\\\\c8285903-c70f-45c9-bcd0-9f33e5af1636\\\\agents\\\\6e2da8f4-5d72-496a-b081-0298149135c0\\\\instructions\\\\AGENTS.md\",\"time\":{\"start\":1774925848365,\"end\":1774925848369}}}}\r\n{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1774925848422,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2be2e7ec3ffe2J1yV1v8pTHnpE\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d41d31f65001tnHgYjXm8YQQ3A\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d41d30474001U9BWkv9YvJJKMs\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2be2e7ec3ffe2J1yV1v8pTHnpE\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":39894,\"input\":348,\"output\":378,\"reasoning\":0,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":39168}},\"cost\":0}}\r\n{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1774925857755,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2be2e7ec3ffe2J1yV1v8pTHnpE\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d41d343d9001t6r3lbfei8anGG\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d41d31f6a001m4FqkQVwVaTT3Q\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2be2e7ec3ffe2J1yV1v8pTHnpE\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\r\n{\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1774925857759,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2be2e7ec3ffe2J1yV1v8pTHnpE\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d41d343dc002dAxXUAIA0PPWAj\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d41d31f6a001m4FqkQVwVaTT3Q\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2be2e7ec3ffe2J1yV1v8pTHnpE\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"\\n\\nNow I'll create the three hires. First, let me check what workspace I have available.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1774925857757,\"end\":1774925857757}}}\r\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1774925858691,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2be2e7ec3ffe2J1yV1v8pTHnpE\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d41d343de001br9L51SucCFE1O\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d41d31f6a001m4FqkQVwVaTT3Q\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2be2e7ec3ffe2J1yV1v8pTHnpE\",\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"bash\",\"callID\":\"call_function_qssbdza2gapy_1\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"curl.exe -s -H \\\"Authorization: Bearer $env:PAPERCLIP_API_KEY\\\" \\\"$env:PAPERCLIP_API_URL/api/projects