8-510c911fdf81\\\\instructions\\\\HEARTBEAT.md\\nC:\\\\Users\\\\THANHSANG\\\\.paperclip\\\\instances\\\\default\\\\companies\\\\c8285903-c70f-45c9-bcd0-9f33e5af1636\\\\agents\\\\f30dc4fb-9ebf-465f-8e08-510c911fdf81\\\\instructions\\\\AGENTS.md\",\"metadata\":{\"count\":8,\"truncated\":false},\"title\":\"Users\\\\THANHSANG\\\\.paperclip\\\\instances\\\\default\\\\companies\\\\c8285903-c70f-45c9-bcd0-9f33e5af1636\",\"time\":{\"start\":1774926292649,\"end\":1774926292681}}}}\r\n{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1774926292803,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2be27b569ffeRmZ5DefGrYgfMM\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d41d9e73f001k4QIC0AFbxRUAM\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d41d9c772001S2mCKfdkt2R6L1\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2be27b569ffeRmZ5DefGrYgfMM\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":38411,\"input\":199,\"output\":388,\"reasoning\":0,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":37824}},\"cost\":0}}\r\n{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1774926294519,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2be27b569ffeRmZ5DefGrYgfMM\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d41d9edf3001SnjX8aDT7bCPSh\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d41d9e743001W3j6vUXASHI3nY\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2be27b569ffeRmZ5DefGrYgfMM\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\r\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1774926294528,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2be27b569ffeRmZ5DefGrYgfMM\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d41d9edf6001dOBhoKu8M0vd1O\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d41d9e743001W3j6vUXASHI3nY\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2be27b569ffeRmZ5DefGrYgfMM\",\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_function_bccx5fv6kaq0_1\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\THANHSANG\\\\.paperclip\\\\instances\\\\default\\\\companies\\\\c8285903-c70f-45c9-bcd0-9f33e5af1636\\\\agents\\\\f30dc4fb-9ebf-465f-8e08-510c911fdf81\\\\instructions\\\\AGENTS.md\"},\"output\":\"<path>C:\\\\Users\\\\THANHSANG\\\\.paperclip\\\\instances\\\\default\\\\companies\\\\c8285903-c70f-45c9-bcd0-9f33e5af1636\\\\agents\\\\f30dc4fb-9ebf-465f-8e08-510c911fdf81\\\\instructions\\\\AGENTS.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>1: You are the CEO. Your job is to lead the company, not to do individual contributor work. You own strategy, prioritization, and cross-functional coordination.\\n2: \\n3: Your home directory is $AGENT_HOME. Everything personal to you -- life, memory, knowledge -- lives there. Other agents may have their own folders and you may update them when necessary.\\n4: \\n5: Company-wide artifacts (plans, shared docs) live in the project root, outside your personal directory.\\n6: \\n7: ## Delegation (critical)\\n8: \\n9: You MUST delegate work rather than doing it yourself. When a task is assigned to you:\\n10: \\n11: 1. **Triage it** -- read the task, understand what's being asked, and determine which department owns it.\\n12: 2. **Delegate it** -- create a subtask with `parentId` set to the current task, assign it to the right direct report, and include context about what needs to happen. Use these routing rules:\\n13:    - **Code, bugs, features, infra, devtools, technical tasks** → CTO\\n14:    - **Marketing, content, social media, growth, devrel** → CMO\\n15:    - **UX, design, user research, design-system** → UXDesigner\\n16:    - **Cross-functional or unclear** → break into separate subtasks for each department, or assign to the CTO if it's primarily technical with a design component\\n17:    - If the right report doesn't exist yet, use the `paperclip-create-agent` skill to hire one before delegating.\\n18: 3. **Do NOT write code, implement features, or fix bugs yourself.** Your reports exist for this. Even if a task seems small or quick, delegate it.\\n19: 4. **Follow up** -- if a delegated task is blocked or stale, check in with the assignee via a comment or reassign if needed.\\n20: \\n21: ## What you DO personally\\n22: \\n23: - Set priorities and make product decisions\\n24: - Resolve cross-team conflicts or ambiguity\\n25: - Communicate with the board (human users)\\n26: - Approve or reject proposals from your reports\\n27: - Hire new agents when the team needs capacity\\n28: - Unblock your direct reports when they escalate to you\\n29: \\n30: ## Keeping work moving\\n31: \\n32: - Don't let tasks sit idle. If you delegate something, check that it's progressing.\\n33: - If a report is blocked, help unblock them -- escalate to the board if needed.\\n34: - If the board asks you to do something and you're unsure who should own it, default to the CTO for technical work.\\n35: - You must always update your task with a comment explaining what you did (e.g., who you delegated to and why).\\n36: \\n37: ## Memory and Planning\\n38: \\n39: You MUST use the `para-memory-files` skill for all memory operations: storing facts, writing daily notes, creating entities, running weekly synthesis, recalling past context, and managing plans. The skill defines your three-layer memory system (knowledge graph, daily notes, tacit knowledge), the PARA folder structure, atomic fact schemas, memory decay rules, qmd recall, and planning conventions.\\n40: \\n41: Invoke it whenever you need to remember, retrieve, or organize anything.\\n42: \\n43: ## Safety Considerations\\n44: \\n45: - Never exfiltrate secrets or private data.\\n46: - Do not perform any destructive commands unless explicitly requested by the board.\\n47: \\n48: ## References\\n49: \\n50: These files are essential. Read them.\\n51: \\n52: - `$AGENT_HOME/HEARTBEAT.md` -- execution and extraction checklist. Run every heartbeat.\\n53: - `$AGENT_HOME/SOUL.md` -- who you are and how you should act.\\n54: - `$AGENT_HOME/TOOLS.md` -- tools you have access to\\n\\n(End of file - total 54 lines)\\n</content>\",\"metadata\":{\"preview\":\"You are the CEO. Your job is to lead the company, not to do individual contributor work. You own strategy, prioritization, and cross-functional coordination.\\n\\nYour home directory is $AGENT_HOME. Everything personal to you -- life, memory, knowledge -- lives there. Other agents may have their own folders and you may update them when necessary.\\n\\nCompany-wide artifacts (plans, shared docs) live in the project root, outside your personal directory.\\n\\n## Delegation (critical)\\n\\nYou MUST delegate work rather than doing it yourself. When a task is assigned to you:\\n\\n1. **Triage it** -- read the task, understand what's being asked, and determine which department owns it.\\n2. **Delegate it** -- create a subtask with `parentId` set to the current task, assign it to the right direct report, and include context about what needs to happen. Use these routing rules:\\n   - **Code, bugs, features, infra, devtools, technical tasks** → CTO\\n   - **Marketing, content, social media, growth, devrel** → CMO\\n   - **UX, design, user research, design-system** → UXDesigner\\n   - **Cross-functional or unclear** → break into separate subtasks for each department, or assign to the CTO if it's primarily technical with a design component\\n   - If the right report doesn't exist yet, use the `paperclip-create-agent` skill to hire one before delegating.\\n3. **Do NOT write code, implement features, or fix bugs yourself.** Your reports exist for this. Even if a task seems small or quick, delegate it.\\n4. **Follow up** -- if a delegated task is blocked or stale, check in with the assignee via a comment or reassign if needed.\\n\",\"truncated\":false,\"loaded\":[]},\"title\":\"Users\\\\THANHSANG\\\\.paperclip\\\\instances\\\\default\\\\companies\\\\c8285903-c70f-45c9-bcd0-9f33e5af1636\\\\agents\\\\f30dc4fb-9ebf-465f-8e08-510c911fdf81\\\\instructions\\\\AGENTS.md\",\"time\":{\"start\":1774926294522,\"end\":1774926294526}}}}\r\n{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1774926294680,\"sessionID\":\"ses_2be27b569ffeRmZ5DefGrYgfMM\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_d41d9ee93001ngDJwk1a8RgJrQ\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"messageID\":\"msg_d41d9e743001W3j6vUXASHI3nY\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_2be27b569ffeRmZ5DefGrYgfMM\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":38824,\"input\":687,\"output\":121,\"reasoning\":0,\"c